# Daybook — what does not belong in version control.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY SHOULD STAY PRIVATE.
# tools/release.ps1 carries the deployment target in plain text: the SSH host alias,
# the remote document-root path, and the live site URL — someone
# else's business site that Daybook is published into a subfolder of. Publishing this
# repo would hand out a map of that server. Nothing here is a secret in the
# credential sense (SSH keys live in ~/.ssh and are never in the tree), but the
# hostnames, paths and URLs are infrastructure detail about a third party's site.
#
# There is genuinely little else to exclude. Zero dependencies, runtime and dev, so
# no node_modules. No build step, so no build output — tools/stamp-sw.mjs edits sw.js
# in place and that edit is committed. tools/release.ps1 stages into the system temp
# directory, never into the tree. Everything below is either machine cruft or
# something that must never be committed by accident.

# --- Her diary. The one rule here that matters. -------------------------------
# Exports are her backup and her exit (B6), and they are a named person's health
# record (B3). They belong in her downloads folder, never in a repository. These
# match what the app actually writes: daybook-backup-<date>.json and
# daybook-<date>.csv. If one is ever dropped in here to inspect, git will not see it.
daybook-backup-*.json
daybook-*.csv
*.export.json

# And the same rule for readings from anywhere else. A mySugr export turned up in
# the working directory on 2026-08-10 - untracked, not ignored, one `git add -A`
# from being committed - with Blood Sugar Measurement and insulin columns in it.
# The rule was never "our exports"; it is "nobody's readings", and hers may well
# arrive from the app her meter came with rather than from this one.
# Deliberately broad. Anything genuinely meant for the repo can be forced in with
# `git add -f`, which is a decision someone makes on purpose.
mySugr_Export_*.csv
*[Ee]xport*.csv
*[Ee]xport*.json
*glucose*.csv
*readings*.csv

# --- The deploy target. The one file that must never be committed. -------------
# tools/release.local.ps1 holds the SSH alias, remote folder and public URL of a
# third party's server. The script refuses to run without it; the example beside
# it is committed and shows the shape. This repo has a public mirror, and the
# mirror must not know the target exists.
tools/release.local.ps1

# --- Machine-local Claude Code settings ---------------------------------------
# .claude/settings.json IS committed — it is part of the constitution. The .local
# variant is per-machine override and is not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows is the host; macOS entries are here for anyone who ever clones it.
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*

# --- Editors ------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Node ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Should never appear — package.json declares no dependencies of either kind and
# `npm test` runs node --test directly. Present as a guard, not an expectation.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/make-icons.py is run by hand; `npm run dev` is python -m http.server.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- Transient ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tgz
*.tmp
daybook-release-*/
